{"step_index":149,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-04T21:53:39Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-05T03:23:39+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-05T03:23:39+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/config/skills/nexlev-mcp-caller/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 130\nTotal Bytes: 5567\nShowing lines 1 to 130\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: nexlev-mcp-caller\n3: description: >-\n4:   Calls NexLev MCP tools directly via Python + mcp SDK when the built-in\n5:   call_mcp_tool fails or NexLev server is not found. ALWAYS activate when\n6:   the user says \"use nexlev\", \"call nexlev\", \"nexlev mcp\", \"get channel\n7:   analytics via nexlev\", \"check monetization via nexlev\", \"find similar\n8:   channels\", \"nexlev not working\", \"nexlev auth\", or \"fix nexlev\". Also\n9:   activate when call_mcp_tool returns \"server name nexlev not found\".\n10:   Contains ready-to-run Python scripts in the scripts/ subfolder —\n11:   NEVER rewrite these scripts, just import and call them.\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # nexlev-mcp-caller\n15: \n16: Call NexLev MCP tools directly using pre-built Python scripts when the\n17: built-in `call_mcp_tool` tool fails (returns \"server not found\" or errors).\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## CRITICAL: DO NOT REWRITE THE SCRIPTS\n22: \n23: The `scripts/` folder contains production-ready Python files. You MUST:\n24: 1. Use them AS-IS — do not recreate or rewrite them\n25: 2. Call them via `python <script_path> <tool_name> <args_file>`\n26: 3. Only create small temporary JSON arg files when needed\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## Quick Start — How To Call Any NexLev Tool\n31: \n32: ### Step 1: Create a JSON args file (temp)\n33: \n34: ```powershell\n35: # Write args to a temp file (avoids PowerShell JSON mangling)\n36: Set-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_args.json\" -Value '{\"username\": \"EverythingProfessor\"}'\n37: ```\n38: \n39: ### Step 2: Run the caller script\n40: \n41: ```powershell\n42: python \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_call.py\" youtube_channel_about \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_args.json\"\n43: ```\n44: \n45: ### Step 3: Parse the JSON output\n46: \n47: The script prints raw JSON text from NexLev. Parse it for your report.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## For Multiple Tool Calls (Batch Mode)\n52: \n53: Use the batch script to call multiple tools in one run:\n54: \n55: ```powershell\n56: # Create a batch config file\n57: Set-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_batch.json\" -Value '[\n58:   {\"tool\": \"youtube_channel_about\", \"args\": {\"username\": \"SomeChannel\"}},\n59:   {\"tool\": \"youtube_channel_videos\", \"args\": {\"channel_id\": \"UC...\", \"sort_by\": \"popular\"}},\n60:   {\"tool\": \"check_channel_monetization\", \"args\": {\"channelId\": \"UC...\"}}\n61: ]'\n62: \n63: python \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_batch.py\" \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_batch.json\"\n64: ```\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## Available Scripts\n69: \n70: | Script | Purpose |\n71: |--------|---------|\n72: | `scripts/nexlev_call.py` | Call a single NexLev tool by name + args file |\n73: | `scripts/nexlev_batch.py` | Call multiple NexLev tools sequentially |\n74: | `scripts/nexlev_kill_stale.py` | Kill stale mcp-remote processes blocking port 28085 |\n75: \n76: ---\n77: \n78: ## NexLev Rate Limits (Free Plan) — CHECK BEFORE CALLING\n79: \n80: | Limit | Tools |\n81: |-------|-------|\n82: | **50/day** | youtube_search, youtube_channel_videos, youtube_channel_shorts, youtube_channel_playlists, youtube_channel_about |\n83: | **20/day** | latest_discovered_faceless_niches, search_youtube_suggested_videos, search_viral_videos_small_channels, faceless_outliers_videos |\n84: | **10/day** | channel_resolver, search_niche_finder_channels, search_videos, youtube_video_details, youtube_video_comments, youtube_channel_outliers, find_long_form_channels, find_shorts_channels, get_niche_finder_categories, get_niche_finder_formats |\n85: | **5/day** | get_similar_channels, check_faceless_channel, get_similar_videos, get_video_transcript, get_bulk_video_transcripts, get_video_subtitle, get_bulk_video_subtitles, get_similar_thumbnails, get_channel_analytics, get_daily_analytics, get_short_vs_long_views, get_geography_revenue, get_batch_channel_metrics, check_channel_monetization, check_video_monetization, get_video_rpm, get_niche_overview, get_niche_finder_tags, get_channel_promotions |\n86: | **2/day** | get_channel_promotions_realtime |\n87: | **1/day** | watch_youtube_video_and_ask, watch_instagram_video_and_ask, watch_tiktok_video_and_ask |\n88: | **0/day (Paid only)** | get_content_owner, search_cms_networks, swipefile tools, my_channel tools, generate/edit_thumbnail |\n89: \n90: ### Rate Limit Strategy\n91: 1. **ALWAYS start with 50/day tools** (youtube_channel_about → youtube_channel_videos)\n92: 2. **Use 5/day tools sparingly** — ask the user before burning get_channel_analytics\n93: 3. **If RATE LIMIT EXCEEDED** — tell the user which tool, suggest waiting 24h or enabling NexLev usage credits\n94: \n95: ### Full rate limit reference file\n96: `C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\Nexlev's official rate-limt mcp.md`\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: ## Troubleshooting\n101: \n102: | Problem | Fix |\n103: |---------|-----|\n104: | `server name nexlev not found` from call_mcp_tool | Use this skill's Python scripts instead |\n105: | `RATE LIMIT EXCEEDED` | Check table above. Wait 24h or enable credits at nexlev.io |\n106: | Auth window doesn't open / \"Another instance running\" | Run `nexlev_kill_stale.py` then retry |\n107: | `Connection closed` | Stale mcp-remote process. Run `nexlev_kill_stale.py` then retry |\n108: | First time ever / tokens expired | Browser auth window will open automatically — complete it |\n109: | `npx` not found | Scripts already use `npx.cmd` — this is handled |\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: ## OAuth Token Cache\n114: \n115: After first browser authorization, tokens are cached at:\n116: - `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.mcp-auth\\` (or similar npm cache location)\n117: - Tokens survive across conversations — you only auth once\n118: \n119: ---\n120: \n121: ## Channel Workflow Template\n122: \n123: Standard workflow for analyzing a channel:\n124: \n125: 1. `youtube_channel_about` (50/day) → Get channel ID, subs, views, join date, links\n126: 2. `youtube_channel_videos` with `sort_by: \"popular\"` (50/day) → Top videos\n127: 3. `check_channel_monetization` (5/day) → Monetized?\n128: 4. `check_faceless_channel` (5/day) → Faceless?\n129: 5. `get_channel_analytics` (5/day) → Growth, revenue estimates — **save this for last, only if needed**\n130: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
